Z||000000||Motorhead||03-28-2000||08:16 AM||||<BR>So far we seem to have four people interested in forming a Carolina Fiero club.  Not a bad start!  You folks in Ohio seem to have a great group, how 'bout some suggestions on how us "good ole' boys" can get started.  NIFE, Illinois or Indiana.  Sorry, can't remember which state.  Y'all seem to have your act together also.  Any and all suggestions greatly appreciated.<BR>It's a sunny and warm day here in SC, think I'll go Fieroing!<BR>Shorts and sandals mandatory!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carolina 88GT||03-29-2000||08:08 AM||||Just remember......If we do this thing...I absolutely refuse to be refered to as the Good Ol' Boy Fiero Club.  I cant get a gun rack in my rear window, a hound dog wont fit in my "bed" and I have a terrible dislike for RC Cola and fried porkskins.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||03-29-2000||08:58 AM||||Well, I have gotten the Ashland-Mansfield Fiero Club off the ground (4 members so far with 8 cars) by getting my name and number in the forth quarter FOCOA mag. (1 guy from there)And by Printing up some flyers about the club and sticking them under Fiero wiper blades that I find parked and posting the flyers around town in Parts stores,Auto Dealerships, etc. As far as the OHIO connection goes I believe that 87ECO5 is mostly responsible...lol Just plan something (cookout,rally,scavenger hunt,whatever) and post it here and, maybe, in some local newspapers. "IF YOU BUILD IT - THEY WILL COME"||||reg||14
Z||000003||bHooper||03-29-2000||11:22 AM||||yes!  i am against anything that would be called the "good ol'boy" or "nascar" anything club... but i will happilly bring the pork rinds and rc/cherwine to the first meeting.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>speeking of which, this might actually become a logistical nightmare with everyone as spread out as we are ||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||03-29-2000||02:16 PM||||Yep, lets do it! Just yesterday I saw several more Fieros that I've ever seen in one day. A silver 86SE that needed attention everywhere! Two red coupes on highway 17. A while ago, I had cards made up with my phone number on then and my Fieroholic mechanic's phone number on too. Well, he's still repairing Fieros, but he lost his shop (divorce). So he's pretty much working beside his house until he gets his 86GT Ferrari Dino sold. <BR>I've been thinking about putting Pennock's Fiero Forum and my email address or phone number on new ones. The Carolina Fiero Club name would be on the top. What would we name it? I agree, bhooper, nothing that resembles NASCAR!<BR>A friend of mine said: the north has the maffia, the south has nascar! LOL<P>If we can come up with a name, LMK, and I'll have cards made up, and can mail a couple hundred or two to ya! Lets get it rolling!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Motorhead||03-30-2000||07:03 PM||||Commited a real faux pax with the "good 'ole boys" remark, sorry about that guys, I'm no NASCAR fan either.<P>Hey Turbo, I drive a red coupe, might have been me.  I passed a burgandy GT yesterday near Marion. <P>Maybe if we planned something in a central location, with a date far enough in advance, we could more easily make arrangements for everyone to be there.<P>As far as a name, how 'bout the subject of this post?<P>CAROLINA FIEROS'||||reg||1
Z||000006||Motorhead||03-30-2000||07:34 PM||||Well,put pins where everone is on the map.  Even found Pikeville!<BR>Looks like Fayettevile is the most central location, about an hour and a half from me.  Maybe less.<P>How about if everyone picks a weekend in April, and one in May, that would be free for them, and we'll see if we get any matches.  I know April is tough with Easter in there.  I think I have a divorce scheduled for that month also.  But what the heck, give it a shot!||||reg||1
